# InstallTool.action
#
# The ROS2-action form of problog_project's InstallTool BT node (see
# module/contracts/schema.yaml's own InstallTool entry). An action, not
# a service like TakeSample, because it's DURATIVE -- same start/halt
# shape as MoveTo.action, a fixed-Duration analogue of one
# startMoveto/haltMoveto pair, just without the continuous trajectory
# (the robot never moves during this action).
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' tool_action_node, which runs this for
# `tool`'s own configured Duration (this problem's own config.yaml,
# tool.install.duration_seconds.<tool>), halting early on whichever of
# `triggers` fires first (battery-only -- see that port's own
# description below), or resolving a success/failure coin flip
# (tool.install.success_probability) once the full Duration elapses
# with nothing halting it early. On success, tool_action_node updates
# its own tracked "currently equipped tool" state (published on the
# latched `tool_state` topic) -- see move_to_node.py's own note on how
# that changes a SUBSEQUENT MoveTo's speed, and battery_sim_node's own
# note on how it changes moving_drain_rate.

# "cart" or "plow" -- the ONLY two tool kinds accepted.
string tool

# EXTRA halting conditions -- OPTIONAL, may be omitted or empty.
# RESTRICTED to battery-related names ONLY: battery_below(Threshold),
# battery_equal(Threshold), battery_over(Threshold) (see MoveTo.action's
# own triggers port for what each means -- identical semantics, just
# checked against the IDLE drain rate's own reading, since this action
# never moves the robot). A motion-based name is not supported --
# tool_action_node ignores it with a warning rather than a hard error,
# there being no translation-time validation pass in this simulation
# the way schema.yaml itself describes for the formal ProbLog pipeline.
string[] triggers
---
# Result

# "install_success"/"install_failure" if the full Duration elapsed
# (matching TakeSample's own bare "sample_success"/"sample_failure"
# shape, not schema.yaml's literal install_tool_success(Tool,ActionCode)
# Prolog term text -- same adaptation MoveTo's own "completed" reason
# already makes), or the name of whichever battery trigger fired first
# (e.g. "battery_below(20)") if one did.
string reason

# true iff reason is "install_success".
bool status
---
# Feedback

# Wall-clock seconds elapsed since this action started.
float64 elapsed_s
